use std
into codec_webp.amni

Namespace codec_webp. Decodes WebP still pictures to RGBA8 (4 bytes per pixel, top row first): lossy VP8 with or without an ALPH alpha chunk, lossless VP8L, in the simple and the extended (VP8X) RIFF container. The result matches libwebp's `WebPDecodeRGBA` byte for byte: colors are not premultiplied and alpha is 255 when the file has none. Nothing here may crash, loop forever or read past the end of damaged data: every read is checked, every index is checked before it is used, and any problem makes `decode` give false with a short reason kept for `error()`. Whole numbers are 64-bit `int`; "arithmetic shift" means the shift that rounds toward minus infinity on negative numbers; "C division" truncates toward zero. Module state is reused between calls so a decode allocates nothing once the lists have grown.

